ed}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThis implies that the given line passes through the point $P(2,-3,7)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨4,5,-6⟩.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-2}{4}=\\frac{y-(-3)}{5}=\\frac{z-7}{-6}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-2}{4}=\\frac{y+3}{5}=\\frac{z-7}{-6}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360845 #edb/ref 1080 "images/31/31519aa878fd6a9b450296552afd9bbf628e30db68a2d7c6dc6b02a48ae28b06.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360845 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360845 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "037a7d4f-c46b-5ef5-9f12-e499f543ede1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360849 #edb/ref 1080 "images/a3/a375a537b104f5bcdd8f5951277bce2494d8861a7212772a7d7050fa14091cb9.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360849 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360849 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0562a68a-9113-579a-9191-136bc8b91243" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360894 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360894 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360894 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "10267759-948c-5e21-b819-eea0a52b9c53" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360984 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360984 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360984 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "21c0f117-930c-5f72-bd6c-e01d53d016cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361050 #edb/ref 1080 "images/d7/d72110682c1959f10546b6fa49d6e4ebedf6b6d5557639c772f28a920f306df5.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361050 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361050 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2f9fb8a